.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
Interface routines with extended capabilities\&. 


.SH "Typedef Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "typedef sc_uint128_t \fBp8est_lid_t\fP"

.PP
A datatype to handle the linear id in 3D\&. We use the implementation of unsigned 128 bit integer in libsc, i\&.e\&., a struct with the members high_bits and low_bits (both uint64_t)\&. 
.SS "typedef void(* p8est_replace_t) (\fBp8est_t\fP *\fBp8est\fP, \fBp4est_topidx_t\fP which_tree, int num_outgoing, \fBp8est_quadrant_t\fP *outgoing[], int num_incoming, \fBp8est_quadrant_t\fP *incoming[])"

.PP
Callback function prototype to replace one set of quadrants with another\&. This is used by extended routines when the quadrants of an existing, valid \fBp8est\fP are changed\&. The callback allows the user to make changes to newly initialized quadrants before the quadrants that they replace are destroyed\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fI\fBp8est\fP\fP A valid forest for context\&. 
.br
\fIwhich_tree\fP Tree index of the invocation\&. 
.br
\fInum_outgoing\fP The number of outgoing quadrants\&. 
.br
\fIoutgoing\fP The outgoing quadrants: after the callback, the user_data, if \fIp8est->data_size\fP is nonzero, will be destroyed\&. 
.br
\fInum_incoming\fP The number of incoming quadrants\&. 
.br
\fIincoming\fP The incoming quadrants: prior to the callback, the user_data, if \fIp8est->data_size\fP is nonzero, is allocated, and the p8est_init_t callback, if it has been provided, will be called\&.
.RE
.PP
If the mesh is being refined, num_outgoing will be 1 and num_incoming will be 8, and vice versa if the mesh is being coarsened\&. 
.SH "Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "void p8est_balance_ext (\fBp8est_t\fP * p8est, \fBp8est_connect_type_t\fP btype, \fBp8est_init_t\fP init_fn, \fBp8est_replace_t\fP replace_fn)"

.PP
2:1 balance the size differences of neighboring elements in a forest\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fI\fBp8est\fP\fP The \fBp8est\fP to be worked on\&. 
.br
\fIbtype\fP Balance type (face, edge, or corner/full)\&. Corner balance is almost never required when discretizing a PDE; just causes smoother mesh grading\&. 
.br
\fIinit_fn\fP Callback function to initialize the user_data which is already allocated automatically\&. 
.br
\fIreplace_fn\fP Callback function that allows the user to change incoming quadrants based on the quadrants they replace\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void p8est_coarsen_ext (\fBp8est_t\fP * p8est, int coarsen_recursive, int callback_orphans, \fBp8est_coarsen_t\fP coarsen_fn, \fBp8est_init_t\fP init_fn, \fBp8est_replace_t\fP replace_fn)"

.PP
Coarsen a forest\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fI\fBp8est\fP\fP The forest is changed in place\&. 
.br
\fIcoarsen_recursive\fP Boolean to decide on recursive coarsening\&. 
.br
\fIcallback_orphans\fP Boolean to enable calling coarsen_fn even on non-families\&. In this case, the second quadrant pointer in the argument list of the callback is NULL, subsequent pointers are undefined, and the return value is ignored\&. If coarsen_recursive is true, it is possible that a quadrant is called once or more as an orphan and eventually becomes part of a family\&. With coarsen_recursive false and callback_orphans true, it is guaranteed that every quadrant is passed exactly once into the coarsen_fn callback\&. 
.br
\fIcoarsen_fn\fP Callback function that returns true if a family of quadrants shall be coarsened\&. 
.br
\fIinit_fn\fP Callback function to initialize the user_data which is already allocated automatically\&. 
.br
\fIreplace_fn\fP Callback function that allows the user to change incoming quadrants based on the quadrants they replace\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBp8est_t\fP* p8est_copy_ext (\fBp8est_t\fP * input, int copy_data, int duplicate_mpicomm)"

.PP
Make a deep copy of a \fBp8est\fP\&. The connectivity is not duplicated\&. Copying of quadrant user data is optional\&. If old and new data sizes are 0, the user_data field is copied regardless\&. The inspect member of the copy is set to NULL\&. The revision counter of the copy is set to zero\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIinput\fP Valid forest to return a copy of\&. 
.br
\fIcopy_data\fP If true, data are copied\&. If false, data_size is set to 0\&. 
.br
\fIduplicate_mpicomm\fP If true, MPI communicator is copied\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
Returns a valid \fBp8est\fP that does not depend on the input, except for borrowing the same connectivity\&. Its revision counter is 0\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void p8est_get_plex_data_ext (\fBp8est_t\fP * p8est, \fBp8est_ghost_t\fP ** ghost, \fBp8est_lnodes_t\fP ** lnodes, \fBp8est_connect_type_t\fP ctype, int overlap, \fBp4est_locidx_t\fP * first_local_quad, sc_array_t * out_points_per_dim, sc_array_t * out_cone_sizes, sc_array_t * out_cones, sc_array_t * out_cone_orientations, sc_array_t * out_vertex_coords, sc_array_t * out_children, sc_array_t * out_parents, sc_array_t * out_childids, sc_array_t * out_leaves, sc_array_t * out_remotes, int custom_numbering)"

.PP
Create the data necessary to create a PETsc DMPLEX representation of a forest, as well as the accompanying lnodes and ghost layer\&. The forest must be at least face balanced (see \fBp4est_balance()\fP)\&. See test/test_plex2\&.c for example usage\&.
.PP
All arrays should be initialized to hold sizeof (p4est_locidx_t), except for \fIout_remotes\fP, which should be initialized to hold (2 * sizeof (p4est_locidx_t))\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fI\fBp8est\fP\fP the forest 
.br
\fIghost\fP the ghost layer 
.br
\fIlnodes\fP the lnodes 
.br
\fIctype\fP the type of adjacency for the overlap 
.br
\fIoverlap\fP the number of layers of overlap (zero is acceptable) 
.br
\fIfirst_local_quad\fP the local quadrants are assigned contiguous plex indices, starting with this index 
.br
\fIout_points_per_dim\fP filled with argument for DMPlexCreateFromDAG() 
.br
\fIout_cone_sizes\fP filled with argument for DMPlexCreateFromDAG() 
.br
\fIout_cones\fP filled with argument for DMPlexCreateFromDAG() 
.br
\fIout_cone_orientations\fP filled with argument for DMPlexCreateFromDAG() 
.br
\fIout_vertex_coords\fP filled with argument for DMPlexCreateFromDAG() 
.br
\fIout_children\fP filled with argument for DMPlexSetTree() 
.br
\fIout_parents\fP filled with argument for DMPlexSetTree() 
.br
\fIout_childids\fP filled with argument for DMPlexSetTree() 
.br
\fIout_leaves\fP filled with argument for PetscSFSetGraph() 
.br
\fIout_remotes\fP filled with argument for PetscSFSetGraph() 
.br
\fIcustom_numbering\fP Whether or use the default numbering (0) of DMPlex child ids or the custom (1)\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void p8est_lid_add (const \fBp8est_lid_t\fP * a, const \fBp8est_lid_t\fP * b, \fBp8est_lid_t\fP * result)"

.PP
Adds the uint128_t \fIb\fP to the uint128_t \fIa\fP\&. \fIresult\fP == \fIa\fP or \fIresult\fP == \fIb\fP is not allowed\&. \fIa\fP == \fIb\fP is allowed\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIa\fP A pointer to a p8est_lid_t\&. 
.br
\fIb\fP A pointer to a p8est_lid_t\&. 
.br
\fIresult\fP A pointer to a p8est_lid_t\&. The sum \fIa\fP + \fIb\fP will be saved in \fIresult\fP\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void p8est_lid_add_inplace (\fBp8est_lid_t\fP * a, const \fBp8est_lid_t\fP * b)"

.PP
Adds the p8est_lid_t \fIb\fP to the p8est_lid_t \fIa\fP\&. The result is saved in \fIa\fP\&. \fIa\fP == \fIb\fP is allowed\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIa\fP A pointer to a p8est_lid_t\&. \fIa\fP will be overwritten by \fIa\fP + \fIb\fP\&. 
.br
\fIb\fP A pointer to a p8est_lid_t\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void p8est_lid_bitwise_and (const \fBp8est_lid_t\fP * a, const \fBp8est_lid_t\fP * b, \fBp8est_lid_t\fP * result)"

.PP
Calculates the bitwise and of the uint128_t \fIa\fP and the uint128_t \fIb\fP\&. \fIa\fP == \fIresult\fP is allowed\&. Furthermore, \fIa\fP == \fIresult\fP and/or \fIb\fP == \fIresult\fP is allowed\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIa\fP A pointer to a p8est_lid_t\&. 
.br
\fIb\fP A pointer to a p8est_lid_t\&. 
.br
\fIresult\fP A pointer to a p8est_lid_t\&. The bitwise and of \fIa\fP and \fIb\fP will be saved\&. in \fIresult\fP\&. 
.RE
.PP

